In article <1488@sirius.ucs.adelaide.edu.au> ganderse@adelphi.ua.oz.au.oz.au (God of Gods) writes:
>        Incidentally, if you eat a dragon egg, do you get the intrinsic
>protection from that dragon (eg shock resistance from eating a blue dragon egg).
>It seems to me that a good trick would be to polymorph into a blue dragon, lay
>an egg, eat the egg when human, then polymorph into the other dragons and eat
>their eggs. An easy way of getting the resistances perhaps, or won't this work?

The eggs (as far as I know) have never given intrinsics.  However, baby 
dragons used to.  This was much abused, and as the dev team is wont to do 
with oft abused quirks of the game (and rightly so - don't get me wrong),
they ended up modifying it so that only adult dragons would give the
resistances.  Thus, it is possible to get all the resistances by laying eggs
in each of the dragon forms, but you have to be extremely patient, waiting
for your baby dragons to grow up before killing and eating them.

